      "topic": "Mortgage servicing",
      "updateType": "Enforcement",
      "title": "State Financial Regulators Reach $15.5 Million Settlement with Mortgage Servicer NewRez, LLC",
      "summary": "Massachusetts announced a 48-state, $15.5 million settlement concerning NewRez\u2019s imposition of force-placed insurance costs on borrowers who already had active homeowners insurance. Massachusetts identifies itself as a lead agency along with Washington, DC, Arkansas, Iowa, and Montana.",
      "publishedDate": "2026-08-12",
      "sourceName": "Massachusetts Division of Banks",
