      "id": "ny-cyber-2026-09-10",
      "agency": "New York DFS",
      "category": "States",
      "state": "New York",
      "topic": "Cybersecurity compliance",
      "updateType": "Guidance",
      "title": "DFS Issues New Cybersecurity Guidance on Risk Assessments for Financial Services Entities",
      "summary": "DFS clarified its existing risk-assessment expectations under its cybersecurity regulation, including scope, frequency, governance, and documentation. Mortgage businesses covered by the regulation should review applicability. DFS states that the guidance does not impose new obligations or requirements.",
